 X syndrome; and STOKE Antisense Oligonucleotide Program, which is in discovery program for SYNGAP1 syndrome. It has a license agreement with Neuren Pharmaceuticals Limited to trofinetide for Rett syndrome and other indications; and a license and collaboration agreement with Stoke Therapeutics, Inc. to discover, develop, and commercialize novel RNA-based medicines for the potential treatment of severe and rare genetic neurodevelopmental diseases of the CNS. The company was formerly known as Receptor Technologies, Inc. and changed its name ACADIA Pharmaceuticals Inc. in 1997. ACADIA Pharmaceuticals Inc. was incorporated in 1993 and is headquartered in San Diego, California.","employees":796,"website":"https://acadia.com","country":"United States","city":"San Diego","officers":[{"name":"Ms. Catherine E. Owen Adams","title":"CEO & Director"},{"name":"Mr. Mark C. Schneyer","title":"Executive VP & CFO"},{"name":"Ms. Jennifer J. Rhodes J.D.","title":"Executive VP, Chief Legal Officer & Secretary"}]},"sector_medians":{"fpe":19.16,"tpe":30.0,"ps":4.313,"pfcf":28.56,"peg":1.36,"pb":4.486,"ev_ebitda":16.71,"rev_growth":0.097,"eps_growth":0.154,"eps_growth_fwd":0.0934,"eps_growth_next":0.1096,"div_yield":0,"roe":0.02656,"roa":0.02473,"de":43.27,"gross_margin":0.4983,"op_margin":0.0549,"profit_margin":0,"current_ratio":2.993},"valuation":[{"k":"fpe","label":"Forward P/E","v":15.77,"sector":19.16,"verdict":"Fairly valued"},{"k":"tpe","label":"TTM P/E","v":7.783,"sector":30.0,"verdict":"Undervalued"},{"k":"ps","label":"Price / Sales","v":2.372,"sector":4.313,"verdict":"Undervalued"},{"k":"pfcf","label":"Price / FCF","v":61.63,"sector":28.56,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"peg","label":"PEG","v":null,"sector":1.36,"verdict":"—"},{"k":"pb","label":"Price / Book","v":2.055,"sector":4.486,"verdict":"Undervalued"},{"k":"de","label":"Debt / Equity (%)","v":5.179,"sector":43.27,"verdict":"Low debt"},{"k":"rev_growth","label":"Revenue growth","v":0.228,"sector":0.097,"verdict":"Strong"},{"